% core_attunement - what a fight needs, and the roles that make it a team
%
% Top-down: a strategy needs an enemy blasted dead, or struck dead, or
% exposed. These methods say what would work (a reaction that blasts
% lethally, a strike element the enemy is not immune to) and hand the
% ingredients to core_chemistry, which finds who holds them.
%
% GDD 2: no single entity overcomes a significant challenge alone. Here that
% is a *role* rule, not an identity rule: whoever primes a region may not be
% the one who pays it off. Any companion can fill either role - the player
% character and the AI companions have the same abilities and differ only by
% who controls them - so cooperation comes from the task's shape, not from a
% fact that names the human. Every pay-off exists in two arities: the bare
% form (anyone), and one taking `?not`, the companion excluded from the role.

% === Rules ===

% Who would prime with ?el: the first companion who can put it down.
primer(?el, ?a) :- first(holder(?el, ?a)).

% === Methods ===

% Prime: put an element on a region. Bare form lets chemistry pick the
% holder; the named form is for a strategy that already assigned the role.
prime(?el, ?r) :- if(), do(castElement(?el, ?r)).
prime(?el, ?r, ?a) :- if(), do(castElementAs(?a, ?el, ?r)).

% The need: whatever stands exposed in ?r is blasted dead. Some element must
% react lethally with the feature there; anyone but ?not casts it.
blastDeadAt(?r) :- if(), do(blastDeadAt(?r, none)).
blastDeadAt(?r, ?not) :-
    if(regionHas(?r, ?feat), blast(?el, ?feat, dead), reacts(?el, ?feat, ?new)),
    do(castElement(?el, ?r, ?not)).

% The need: ?e is struck dead. Some strike element must be lethal and the
% enemy not immune to it; anyone but ?not casts it.
strikeDead(?e) :- if(), do(strikeDead(?e, none)).
strikeDead(?e, ?not) :-
    if(strike(?el, dead), not(immune(?e, ?el))),
    do(strikeElement(?el, ?e, ?not)).

% The need: ?e takes blasts. Already exposed: nothing to do; else some mark
% element drops its guard (a flare in the eyes).
expose(?e) :- if(exposed(?e)), do().
expose(?e) :-
    else, if(role(?e, enemy), mark(?el, ?status), not(immune(?e, ?el))),
    do(markElement(?el, ?e)).
